From: Utkarsh Dalal <utkarsh.dalal@toptal.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:28:58 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] zink: name command buffers only when tracing or capturing

Since 82656de0297b every batch state labels its two command buffers with
vkSetDebugUtilsObjectNameEXT whenever the instance has VK_EXT_debug_utils.
Under gamescope, Xwayland's glamor reaches the container's adrenotools
Turnip through gn-vkshim's proxy, which hands out its own wrapper objects
as VkCommandBuffer handles and passes vkSetDebugUtilsObjectNameEXT through
untouched. Turnip then reads the wrapper as a vk_object_base and faults
(SEGV at 0x58) in the first eglCreateContext, so Xwayland never starts.

The names are only consumed by tracing tools and RenderDoc, so set them
under the same conditions zink already uses for its debug labels. This
can go once the shim unwraps the handle in vkSetDebugUtilsObjectNameEXT.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_batch.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_batch.c b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_batch.c
index 29925bd915ae..8a844932b619 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_batch.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_batch.c
@@ -279,6 +279,13 @@ zink_label_cmd_buffer(struct zink_context *ctx, VkDevice device, VkCommandBuffer
 {
    struct zink_screen *screen = zink_screen(ctx->base.screen);
 
+   bool wanted = zink_tracing;
+#if HAVE_RENDERDOC_INTEGRATION
+   wanted |= screen->renderdoc_api != NULL;
+#endif
+   if (!wanted)
+      return;
+
    VkDebugUtilsObjectNameInfoEXT name_info = {
       .sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_DEBUG_UTILS_OBJECT_NAME_INFO_EXT,
       .pNext = NULL,
